WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.370
Three Gospels, Mark, Matthew
and Luke, tell how Jesus died.

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.330
Each has the darkness, a
centurion, women watching,

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:10.660
and a burial.

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.950
But the last words are
not the same in all three.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.430
In Mark, Jesus cries out: My God, my God,

6
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.840
why have you forsaken me?

7
00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.470
Luke gives him other words entirely.

8
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.950
So do the accounts clash, or
tell one story three ways?

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.400
In this mission, you'll lay the
three accounts side by side,

10
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.770
row by row.

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.400
Then you'll trace the old psalms
and prophecies woven into the story.

12
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:40.310
Your mission: find out whether
the crucifixion accounts clash,

13
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.530
or tell one story three ways.
